 side.\n\nNo public polls or expert ratings cover this presidential contest, so the forecast rests on the state's partisan fundamentals, which point to a Republican edge of roughly six points. Democratic competitiveness in Alaska's down-ballot races, including a tight Senate contest, suggests the state is more contested than its national reputation, but that energy has not historically transferred to top-of-ticket generic matchups. Republicans enter favored, while Democrats would need an unusually favorable national environment to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2436, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3013, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2918, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3121, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2994, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.311, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2901, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2902, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2839, "margin": -6.0}]}